  "description": "This course covers source code security testing techniques, including static analysis tools like SonarQube and Fortify, dynamic analysis using OWASP ZAP and Burp Suite, and penetration testing frameworks such as Metasploit. Students will study secure coding practices, common vulnerabilities like SQL injection and XSS, and mitigation strategies using OWASP Top Ten. Topics include code review methodologies, fuzz testing with AFL, and cryptographic protocol analysis using TLS 1.3 standards. The course also addresses secure deployment practices, container security with Docker, and compliance with ISO 27001 and NIST frameworks. Students will evaluate security testing tools, design test cases for specific vulnerabilities, and implement security testing pipelines for real-world applications.",
